   "state": "OPEN",
   "summary": "source_ref.blobs carries the true 142 distinct blob refs; the controller refuses anything above 133 in three places. No GA can be constructed against this controller until those three literals admit 142.",
   "detail": "R22-F2, reproduced independently on this host. This controller declares 153 REPOSITORY_SOURCE entries which resolve to 142 distinct git blobs once the manifest's own blob is included. source_ref.blobs above carries all 142, because that is the true set and COMPLETE_MANIFEST_FILE_BLOB_COVERAGE in source-publication.mjs requires every declared source file to appear in it. Three separate ceilings of 133 sit inside the FROZEN controller and every one of them refuses this set: context.mjs:113 capacityDelta.source_refs_maximum=133, which the approval and applicability documents must match byte for byte; context.mjs:134 CLOSED_SOURCE_REF_MAXIMUM, a literal blobs.length<=133; and source-publication.mjs:25 COMPLETE_BOUNDED_SOURCE_SET, a literal refs.length<=133. NO GA CAN BE CONSTRUCTED AGAINST CONTROLLER 389fee9b7e533041119838df59706cc2166b44497369cca419b1dc125e9a98ec UNTIL THOSE THREE LITERALS ADMIT AT LEAST 142. Re-issuing the capacity materials alone does NOT achieve that: a new approval carrying source_refs_maximum=160 fails same(a.capacity_delta,capacityDelta) at REAL_EXACT_CAPACITY_APPROVAL_REQUIRED, and the other two ceilings are code, not policy. Raising the ceiling therefore requires a controller change, which contradicts the freeze. This document records the true set rather than a truncated one so the refusal happens at the ceiling, attributably, instead of at COMPLETE_MANIFEST_FILE_BLOB_COVERAGE with a manifest that silently under-declares its own sources."
  },
  {
   "id": "R22-F3",
   "severity": "MAJOR",
   "state": "OPEN",
   "summary": "The computed load set follows one edge type out of five (round 22 section 4). selftest-runtime-pins.mjs reports its census as 73 digest literals over 56 statically reachable modules, and that denominator inherits the same single-edge derivation. Deliberately left open by the Owner to make the window; named here so it is not discovered later."
  },
  {
   "id": "R22-F5",
   "severity": "MODERATE",
   "state": "OPEN",
   "summary": "HostProvisioning.json does not describe the node_modules requirement. Verified on this host: with apps/clued-cloud/node_modules absent, selftest-runtime-pins.mjs fails two items (the pristine trusted-entry probe and the per-file byte check) with FileNotFoundError on apps/clued-cloud/node_modules/ajv/lib/ajv.js, and the attribution rule in HostProvisioning.json does not cover it. Installing ajv 6.15.0 there cleared both."
  },
  {
   "id": "R22-F6",
